{
  "version": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "serial-port",
    "description": "Serial byte-stream + framing demo - no Python. A Sources.Iterator counter drives Bytes.Pack (auto-emit on each step), which assembles a fixed 4-byte record [len=3, count, 0x2A '*', 0x0A LF] (the three constants come from the 'defaults' block, the counter is wired). That record is sent out 'serial-tx' (COM3); 'serial-rx' (COM4) reads the stream and Framer.Fixed (frameSize 4) reassembles each 4-byte record, which Bytes.Unpack decodes (count at byte offset 1). Two Debug.ValueDisplay nodes show the raw packed bytes and the reframed bytes. Covers Serial.Port (x2), Framer.Fixed, and Bytes.Pack/Unpack. Runs as-is over a com0com COM3<->COM4 virtual pair; for real hardware point 'serial-tx' and 'serial-rx' at your device(s) or use one Serial.Port with a hardware TX-RX loopback. Swap Framer.Fixed for Framer.Delimiter (LF-delimited) or Framer.LengthPrefix (1-byte length) to frame the same stream by separator or length.",
    "authoring": {
      "version": "1.0",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "serial-port",
        "description": "Serial byte-stream + framing demo - no Python. A Sources.Iterator counter drives Bytes.Pack (auto-emit on each step), which assembles a fixed 4-byte record [len=3, count, 0x2A '*', 0x0A LF] (the three constants come from the 'defaults' block, the counter is wired). That record is sent out 'serial-tx' (COM3); 'serial-rx' (COM4) reads the stream and Framer.Fixed (frameSize 4) reassembles each 4-byte record, which Bytes.Unpack decodes (count at byte offset 1). Two Debug.ValueDisplay nodes show the raw packed bytes and the reframed bytes. Covers Serial.Port (x2), Framer.Fixed, and Bytes.Pack/Unpack. Runs as-is over a com0com COM3<->COM4 virtual pair; for real hardware point 'serial-tx' and 'serial-rx' at your device(s) or use one Serial.Port with a hardware TX-RX loopback. Swap Framer.Fixed for Framer.Delimiter (LF-delimited) or Framer.LengthPrefix (1-byte length) to frame the same stream by separator or length."
      },
